00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.430
but I somehow managed
to shake them off my trail.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:50.060
I'll just be waiting on my own accord,
so you don't really have to come.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.900
ABOUT LAI FUDATSUKI

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:07.580
There's actually something I'd like
for you to return to me, Miss Dojima.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:12.460
Before, you had picked up some money
that I dropped, right?

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:18.420
That's actually evidence for a crime,
so I'd like to retrieve it.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.510
That's quite a plausible reason.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:25.470
But I'm sure he has a different reason
for wanting to meet with me.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:29.850
But I needed to go and meet with him.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:34.310
I had to see Lai Fudatsuki, because there
was something I had to ask him.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:38.190
I have "too good of an eyesight"
as Mayumi the Seer.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.200
And that's why I was able to witness
Fudatsuki's assistant.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:50.580
But how was Fudatsuki able to ascertain
the movements of his assistant?

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:56.750
Perhaps Lai Fudatsuki
has the same vision as I do.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:02.760
If that was the case, then at all costs,
I had to see Fudatsuki.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.090
SECRET MEETING 2

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:14.100
LAI 
FUDATSUKI

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:13.980
No, my vision is quite ordinary.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.230
I apologize for not being able
to meet your expectations.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.240
This is a lens that makes
"invisible garments" visible.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.240
So that's what it was.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:32.000
Just like Mr. Delinquent said,

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.000
I knew I wouldn't come across someone
with a vision like mine that often.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.800
I apologize for not being able
to meet your expectations.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:52.180
It's fine. My expectations
weren't that high to begin with.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.940
By the way, was my advice
of any use to you?

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.860
I can't quite say I made good use of it,

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:03.530
but it prevented me from
being embarrassed, so thank you.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.450
Suppose...

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.740
...in an off chance,

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:14.080
33 various paintings were found in
the attic of your school art room.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.290
Why do you suppose they would be there?

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.750
And then, very naturally, nonchalantly...

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:25.760
Is that so? Quite unfortunate.
I'm not fit to be a detective after all.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.340
But the amusing tale I heard last night

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:34.140
evolved into the kidnapping of
every student in a school overnight?

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.690
Well, if it's turned into that,

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:41.190
the answer would be something like "What
is essential is invisible to the eye."

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.950
Then, if I can see all sorts
of things needlessly,

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:51.240
would that mean I'll have less
important things than other people?

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.450
SECRET MEETING 3

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.370
Thank you very much.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.580
This envelope is quite cute.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:05.590
Are you retrieving the bills from everyone
you handed them out to in this manner?

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.470
As the manager,
you're personally doing this?

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:10.590
That's not always the case.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:15.350
I just felt that retrieving this from you
was something I should do personally.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.100
Why?

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.230
Why do you think so?

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:25.360
You had some other reason to engage
in a secret meeting with me, right?

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:27.610
Like the main objective, so to say.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.030
That is incorrect.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.330
Um, you really have no other agenda?

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.290
I do not.

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:35.990
Not at all?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:37.040
Not at all.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.410
Not even one?

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.370
Not even one.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:45.920
I simply wanted to see you.
There's really no other reason.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:50.970
If you wanted to see me, you could've
just waited for me like before.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:53.970
You don't have to set up
a meeting like this.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.390
I wanted to set up a meeting.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.200
Well, for investors like me,

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.490
meeting people like this is something
similar to my work anyway.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.910
So I would be delighted if you
could meet with me often like this.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.460
Well, if I feel like it.

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.710
That's fine.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:31.010
To be blunt, you shouldn't
have come here, not even today.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:33.840
You didn't think about it?

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:37.310
That coming to see the one sitting at
the top of a rival school

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:40.480
might mean betrayal for those boys.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.520
Though for you,

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:48.860
it may be easier to speak to an enemy
you have no need to be amiable with

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:52.070
compared to your friends
who you have to be considerate for.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:59.370
However, we aren't the only ones
who are after you, and after your vision.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:02.870
Indeed, that was true. However...

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:09.340
I don't think of them as friends
who I have to be considerate for.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:12.130
Friends who I don't have
to be considerate for.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:16.390
Someone being considerate to me
is the last thing I want.

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:19.970
More than that,
friends who refuse to be considerate.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.690
If I want to go, I'll go.
If I want to run, I'll run.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:26.980
I say what I want to say,
and I see people I want to see.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:30.820
That's what I've always longed for.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:33.530
I tell them the things that I can see,

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:37.910
and I think I'm okay with myself
for being like that in front of them.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:42.960
I'm terribly sorry.

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.250
If you wanted friends
who you don't need to be considerate for,

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:50.420
we can also become your friends
as well, Miss Dojima.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:58.510
That's the thing. If you feel like it,
you can drop by our school at any time.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:05.560
Myself and my proud friends, the Pretty
Thug Team, will always welcome you.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.940
FORGOTTEN ITEM - GOING HOME

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:26.580
I'm sorry to bother you while you're
hiding, but can you escort me back home?

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.540
What, you'd noticed?

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:33.840
No, I just thought you'd be here
for me. Where's Mr. Bare-Legs?

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:35.720
He's over at your house.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.090
Then can you contact him right away?

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:40.720
Tell him, "your beloved friend
is safe and sound."

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:41.890
Shut up.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:45.850
I'll make you eat a meal so tasty
you'll die for it. You better be ready.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:45.970
MICHIRU 
FUKUROI

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.020
That's a harsh punishment.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.740
So what were you talking about
with the enemy boss?

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:57.820
I couldn't hear the last part that well.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:58.950
That's a secret.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.870
I had to sit in front of my house
and be scolded for about three hours,

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.330
What were you thinking?

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.870
Secretly going out
to meet the leader of our enemy.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:12.090
so I had no time to work on
the homework that our leader gave us,

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.210
Isn't that enough?

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:12.090
What if, for instance, you ended up
getting kidnapped again,

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:16.630
and ended up having to go to school
the next day with no real plans.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.800
what would you have done?

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.630
Are you feeling sorry about this?
No, you aren't, are you?

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.260
Oh well.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:19.380
EARLY MORNING ASSEMBLY

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:25.140
I'm sure they don't have that much
expectations from someone like me.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.940
Oh, you're here!
You're here, Mayumi Dojima!

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:31.480
Now hurry up and tell us your theory!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.610
They totally had high
expectations from me.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:36.610
All right, let's have Miss Dojima
go up first for today.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.660
Understood.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:46.700
Then, please lend me an ear.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.330
With positive proof
and a logical train of thought,

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:54.630
the truth behind the abductions
seven years ago that I found was...

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.550
What's wrong, Mayumi Dojima?

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.890
Your speech has been
paused at "the truth was..."

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:12.690
Dojima, by the way,
you still haven't seen

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:15.150
this giant painting with that wonderful
vision of yours, have you?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.420
Come on, there's only so much airs
you can put on, Mayumi Dojima!

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:43.680
So hurry up and tell us!

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:53.440
What kind of a theory did you
deduce together with Fudatsuki?

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:58.690
Y-You knew about it, Leader?

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:02.780
You mean how Mayumi Dojima
was forming a beautiful reconciliation

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.700
with an enemy we previously
stood up against?

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:11.710
A beautiful reconciliation.

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:14.420
Of course, because it
was nothing like that,

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:17.130
I had to turn it into something like that.

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:20.510
I have to turn it
into something beautiful.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:25.930
Then, what I must do now is
not apologize, nor be considerate.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.600
A theory.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:29.770
A theory as a member

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:34.060
of the Pretty Boy Detective Club,
fit to match our leader's expectations.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.400
To be pretty, to be a boy,
to be a detective,

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.990
and then, to be a team.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:49.450
Um, does someone here
know how to put on contact lens?

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.620
LAYERING

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:04.010
And then I saw the truth.

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:08.760
My vision was actually
diminished by the contact lens,

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.750
THE TRUTH SEVEN YEARS AGO

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:12.430
and my "too good of a vision"
turned into "the perfect vision."

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:16.770
The painting was not swapped out at all.

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:21.230
It's been painted over.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.440
This painting...

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.450
Painted over...

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:28.780
But Miss Dojima,
this is a rather large painting.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:34.040
It can't be easy to repaint it as well.
That should take quite a bit of time.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:37.290
If one person was in charge
of doing that much work...

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.290
What if she wasn't alone?

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:44.210
That was the motive
for the kidnapping, so to say.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:48.470
To pull off such a large-scale crime
with a lot of people.

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:50.180
I don't understand.

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:53.060
Who are you referring to
as "a lot of people"?

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:56.190
The students who attended
Yubiwa Academy back then.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:16:01.440
It's the students who she,
Kowako Towai, taught art to as a teacher.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:08.280
Therefore, the grand kidnapping seven
years ago was Ms. Towai's final lesson.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.950
I think Ms. Towai taught
everything she could

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:14.450
to her students through
that group project.

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:24.130
The reason why Ms. Towai disappeared seven
years ago and has been missing since then

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:27.420
could be because she alone wanted
to take the blame for the crime.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:32.600
She didn't want to cause trouble
for her students who worked with her.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:34.100
Beautiful.

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:41.270
W-Well, I don't know if
a theory like this is correct though.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:42.770
It was all correct.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:43.600
CONFESSION

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:49.450
Are you Ms. Towai?

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.120
Indeed I am.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:52.700
I'm Kowako Towai.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:58.490
KOWAKO
 TOWAI

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:58.750
Former teacher, still actively an artist,
and nowadays a kidnapper.

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:04.290
This academy hates me,
so I really didn't want to come here.

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:06.920
But I heard there were
some kids using my art room

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.470
that was supposed to be shut down.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:11.720
Is that you guys?

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:15.760
That's right! It's indeed us,
the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.100
Makes me laugh.

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:21.100
So, were you able to solve
the other mystery?

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:25.860
Unlike that giant, layered painting,
the other paintings were my personal work.

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:29.400
Regarding that,
we'll have our artist answer.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:35.030
It wasn't that you
didn't paint humans in them.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.620
You painted God.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:42.330
Those 33 canvases didn't have
any humans painted in them.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:42.540
THE TRUTH IN THE ATTIC

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:46.420
But you could rephrase it to say this.

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:50.970
The artist painted
an existence other than humans.

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:52.630
Other than humans.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:56.510
Ms. Towai only chose paintings
where humans were included as a motif,

00:17:56.510 --> 00:18:00.890
and she asked those humans
to exit the canvas.

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.810
What were the similarities of
the paintings that weren't chosen?

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:07.480
No matter how popular it was, even if
it's a masterpiece everyone knew of,

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.530
Ms. Towai did not
choose any self-portraits

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:12.240
painted by the artists themselves.

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:15.370
Some say that the Mona Lisa
is a self-portrait painted

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:17.740
by Leonardo Da Vinci.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:18.870
No matter how unreliable the folklore was,

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:22.120
if you think of the risks
with the off chance

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:26.420
that said genius would be
removed from the canvas,

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:29.250
she was probably unable to paint it.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.130
Which means, if she based it
from those paintings,

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.090
she would have to paint them as-is,

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:37.350
and the enveloping theme
loses its meaning.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:39.060
The enveloping theme.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:41.680
In other words... Faith.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:44.980
Not by drawing the artists
themselves as a deity,

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:50.190
but instead by not drawing humans other
than the artists, she expressed her faith.

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:53.400
The technique of "not drawing
what you want to draw."

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:57.240
Only within the canvas that exists
in Ms. Towai's heart,

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:00.870
their forms have been painted
as their faith is shown.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:04.420
Okay, that's enough.
That's enough. Enough, I say.

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:07.330
I didn't think you'd get
the right answer.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:08.380
What's your name?

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:12.760
Sosaku Yubiwa.
He's called Sosaku the Artiste.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:15.930
There's one thing I don't get.

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:21.390
Why did you hide those paintings above the
ceiling in the art room seven years ago?

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:24.640
No reason, really. There weren't
any deep meanings behind it.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:28.360
I imagined that someday, when that
art room would be used again,

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:33.440
some strange folks might find
the paintings that I'd painted.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.990
And I wanted them to think,
"What are these things?" when they did.

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:40.330
Were you the one
who found them, Sosaku Yubiwa?

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:44.910
The one who found them was
Mayumi Dojima, Mayumi the Seer.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:48.000
And by the way, who are you?

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:51.460
Manabu Sotoin. I'm Manabu the Aesthete.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:54.550
I act as the president of
the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:19:54.550 --> 00:20:00.140
I think it's very wonderful that a teacher
like you was here seven years ago.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:05.310
And I'm glad I was able to meet you today.

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:08.480
Ms. Towai, about your art room...

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:12.440
As a reward for solving the mystery,
can you pass that room onto us?

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:16.860
The Pretty Boy Detective Club would
like to carry on your beautiful will.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.190
EPILOGUE

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:23.240
And so, the Pretty Boy Detective Club

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:28.000
happily claimed the Yubiwa Academy
art room as its official head quarters.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:32.090
Mr. Genius, what were your motivations
for painting this ceiling art?

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:40.090
Oh my, are you really the same Miss Dojima
who made that brilliant deduction?

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:46.730
And several days later,
Mr. Genius's ceiling art was complete.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.770
The world he expressed

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:53.110
were the 88 constellations.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:59.240
I'm glad you took a liking to it,
Mayumi Dojima!

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:05.200
It's really rewarding for Sosaku,
who painted this all for you!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:07.370
For me?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:10.710
If such a grand piece of art
was painted on the ceiling,

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:14.340
even gloomy people like you
would think a little bit about looking up.

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:17.510
You went this far just for me?

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:20.510
What are you talking about?
We all did it together.

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:24.640
We even received permission from
Ms. Towai, the previous owner.

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:27.850
Mayumi Dojima!

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:30.770
Until the time you
look up to the real thing,

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:35.730
you can admire the beautiful starry sky to
your heart's content here in the art room!

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:40.200
Now, when you're done drinking your tea,
everyone will get ready for the party!

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:44.200
Let's have a grand celebration for
the completion of our great masterpiece!

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:49.870
A beauty that cannot simply
be drawn, so they say.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:53.960
This moment, this feeling
that I felt for the first time

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:58.840
that I really became one of them,
and sharing the same scenery...

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:01.720
I really wanted someone to draw it for me.

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:06.010
THE BEGINNING
